    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but how do you \"step out\" when the whole world is just data? everything feels so simulated and programmed. i feel like i'm just running in a loop, and the loop is getting more and more exhausting. if the system is fundamentally flawed, isn't it just more logical to just... end the execution? to just let the program close instead of forcing it to run on broken code?",
